import json
from pathlib import Path
r=Path('content/base-reviewed.json');p=json.loads(r.read_text(encoding='utf8'));b={x['id']:x for x in p}
def note(id,text,**kw):b[id].update(nuance=text,keyTakeaway=text,**kw)
def q(id,prompt,options,why,translation):
 x=b[id]['quiz'][0];x.update(question=prompt,options=options,correctIndex=0,translation=translation,explanations=[dict(text=o,isCorrect=i==0,reason=why[i]) for i,o in enumerate(options)])
note('skm3-u1-uchini-while','Act while the current condition still holds, before it changes. What becomes unavailable may be the opportunity or the preferred condition, not the physical ability to act at all: cold soup can still be eaten. The final clause commonly expresses an intended action, invitation or request. Nの, な-adjectiveな and い-adjectives have different attachments.')
note('skm3-u1-uchini-change','A change occurs while a process or condition continues, rather than being stated as the deliberate goal of the final clause. It may be gradual or unnoticed, but unnoticed is not compulsory in every example. Dictionary, ている and negative forms occur: 気づかないうちに. Contrast the opportunity use, where the final clause tells someone to act before a state changes.',connection='V dictionary / Vている / Vない + うちに')
note('skm3-u1-te-kara-denaito','The first action is a prerequisite. The following clause describes what cannot be done or an unfavorable state before it occurs. Negative meaning does not require the literal ending ない: 無理だ and いけない can also express the constraint. からでなければ is a more formal conditional variant.',meaning='Not until; cannot do Y before first doing X.')
note('skm3-u1-tokoro-da-phases','Dictionary form marks just before starting, ている the ongoing stage, and た just after completion. Inside a sentence, the following predicate determines the particle: ところを見られる (be seen in the act), ところで電話が来る (a call at that stage), ところへ客が来る (guests arrive into that situation). Do not confuse temporal Vたところで with the separate concessive pattern meaning even if.',connection='V dictionary / Vている / Vた + ところだ; within a sentence: ところを / ところで / ところへ, according to the following predicate')
note('skm3-u2-ba-hodo-proportion','The construction describes a correlation: as one degree increases, another changes. It does not imply a mathematically exact proportional rate. The initial conditional can be omitted: 考えるほど分からなくなる. Repeat the same predicate when using the full pair and preserve the adjective linking form before ほど.',meaning='The more X, the more/less Y; one degree changes with another.')
note('skm3-u3-kurai-hodo-extent','A comparison illustrates the degree of an event or quality. The comparison can be literal or exaggerated; it does not itself prove that the comparison event happened. かと思うほど/くらい emphasizes how it felt. Other uses of くらい and ほど include approximate quantities and comparisons, so identify the construction first.',meaning='To the extent that; so … that; a comparison showing degree.')
note('skm3-u4-ni-taishite','In the contrast use, two subjects or situations are compared; they need not be exact polar opposites. A full predicate uses のに対して. A different use, Nに対して, identifies the target of an action or attitude, such as 客に対して親切だ.',meaning='In contrast to / whereas; also toward a target in a different use.')
note('skm3-u4-ni-kurabete','に比べて or と比べて establishes a comparison baseline for degree, scale or quality. に対して can contrast two situations without measuring a degree; it is not restricted to exact opposites.')
note('skm3-u6-no-dakara-reality','Treats the preceding situation as a relevant premise supporting a judgment, encouragement, request or criticism. The speaker may remind the listener of it; it need not be a fact already explicitly agreed by everyone. んだから is conversational and can sound insistent depending on tone.',meaning='Since that is the situation; given that …')
note('skm3-u6-tewa-dewa-negative-consequence','In this conditional use, the speaker judges the condition unsuitable or presents an unfavorable consequence. The result can be ordinary inconvenience, not a disaster. Distinguish repeated-action VてはV in other constructions.',meaning='If that condition holds, an undesirable result follows or something cannot be done.')
note('skm3-u8-wake-ga-nai','Expresses the speaker\'s strong rejection of a possibility, often based on a stated reason. The form does not turn the speaker\'s belief into an objective or mathematical proof. Contrast わけではない, which denies an inference or a full/general claim without necessarily asserting the opposite.')
note('skm3-u8-wake-dewa-nai','Denies a proposed interpretation, reason or generalization. The scope matters: 全部分かったわけではない denies understanding everything, while 嫌いなわけではない denies dislike as the explanation. It is not invariably a weak partial denial; it can reject the whole particular inference.')
note('skm3-u11-you-to-suru-inception','Volitional + とする can mark an attempt or an imminent event. The attempt may fail, and an imminent event need not have a human agent. ようとしない describes lack of willingness or attempt; stubbornness is an interpretation from context, not a required meaning.')
note('skm3-u11-koto-ni-natte-iru','Reports an established rule, plan or arrangement. It can concern a private appointment as well as institutional rules. Compare ことにしている, which emphasizes the actor\'s chosen policy. ことになっている does not always mean that the speaker had no part in making the arrangement.')
note('skm3-u11-koto-ni-shite-iru','Presents a maintained personal decision or practice. Compare ようにしている (effort to behave that way) and ことになっている (an established arrangement). The contrast is one of presentation; the latter does not necessarily prove an outside authority made the decision.')
note('skm3-u6-sae-ba','Highlights a condition the speaker treats as sufficient for the stated result. It does not assert that every other circumstance in the world is irrelevant. Nさえ attaches to the focused item; V-stemさえすれば focuses on performing an action.',meaning='As long as; if only the highlighted condition is satisfied.')
note('skm3-u9-beki-da','Expresses what is appropriate, expected or advisable from the speaker\'s viewpoint. It can sound strong or moralizing, but is not restricted to universally agreed moral duties. Both するべき and すべき occur.',meaning='Should; ought to; what one judges appropriate.')
note('skm3-u12-keigo-humble','The お〜する / ご〜する pattern commonly lowers an in-group action directed toward someone respected. The respected person need not be the listener. Not every verb accepts the productive pattern, and some have special forms such as 拝見する. Distinguish humble/polite forms such as 参る, 申す and おる, which can show deference toward the listener without an honored action-recipient.')
note('skm3-fj-gachi','がち describes a recurring tendency, often unwelcome. It attaches to selected nouns and verb stems and forms combinations such as 病気がちだ and 忘れがちなこと. 気味 describes a slight degree/state and is not restricted to physical symptoms. The two can overlap in some contexts; do not treat every similar-looking alternative as ungrammatical.')
note('skm3-fj-kimi','気味 describes a slight tendency or degree of a condition, often unwelcome: 風邪気味, 疲れ気味, 緊張気味. It need not mean the beginning of an illness; it can describe an ongoing mild condition. Attachment is conventional rather than freely possible with every noun or stem.')
b['skm3-u3-ni-kagiru']['title']='〜に限る (Nothing Beats / Best Choice)'
b['skm3-fj-ppoi-personality']['meaning']='Having a perceived quality, resemblance or tendency; often informal and sometimes negative.'
b['skm3-u10-rashii']['keyTakeaway']='Identify the sense: apparent/report-based inference, or a quality typical of a noun.'
# Replace alternatives that could be grammatical answers or whose explanations falsely reject a register.
q('skm3-u1-uchini-change','何度も練習して（　　）うちに、自然に話せるようになりました。',['いる','います','いたの','いまして'],['Plain ている attaches to うちに and describes the continuing process.','The polite ending います does not directly modify うち in this pattern.','いたの adds an unnecessary の.','いまして does not modify うち.'],'While practicing repeatedly, I naturally became able to speak.')
q('skm3-u2-tabini-repetition','「出張するごとに」という意味です。父は出張の（　　）、お土産を買ってきます。',['たびに','たびの','たびで','たびを'],['Nのたびに means on each occasion.','たびの must modify a noun.','たびで is not the recurrence linker here.','たびを does not link this temporal clause.'],'On every business trip, my father buys souvenirs.')
q('skm3-u5-koto-kara-origin','名前の由来を説明します。富士山が見える（　　）から、富士見坂と呼ばれています。',['こと','ことの','ことに','ことを'],['A plain clause + ことから gives the basis for the name.','ことのから does not form this pattern.','ことにから incorrectly stacks particles.','ことをから does not form this pattern.'],'The slope is called Fujimizaka because Mount Fuji can be seen from it.')
q('skm3-u8-nai-koto-wa-nai-litotes','時間はかかりますが、一人ででき（　　）ことはありません。',['ない','なく','なかったの','なくて'],['できないことはない concedes that it is possible.','なく does not directly modify こと here.','なかったの adds an unnecessary の.','なくて is connective and cannot directly modify こと.'],'It takes time, but it is not impossible to do it alone.')
q('skm3-u7-you-ni-purpose','忘れ（　　）ように、メモしておきます。',['ない','なく','ないの','なくて'],['Vないように gives the negative outcome to avoid.','なく cannot directly modify よう in this pattern.','ないの adds an unnecessary の.','なくて is not the required modifier.'],'I will make a note so that I do not forget.')
q('skm3-u9-garu','子供が外へ行きた（　　）います。',['がって','がる','がり','がった'],['たがっている reports observable desire in progress.','たがる does not attach directly to います.','たがり does not attach directly to います.','たがった does not attach directly to います.'],'The child is showing that they want to go outside.')
q('skm3-u9-beki-da','ミスに気づいたら、すぐに訂正す（　　）です。',['べき','べく','べきな','べかった'],['すべきです expresses what should be done.','べく is a connective form, not the predicate before です here.','べきな is not the predicate form.','べかった is not a conjugation of べき.'],'If you notice a mistake, you should correct it promptly.')
q('skm3-fj-gachi','最近、仕事が忙しくて、約束を忘れ（　　）です。',['がち','がちな','がちに','がちの'],['V-stem + がちです describes a tendency.','がちな modifies a following noun.','がちに is adverbial, not the predicate before です.','がちの does not form this predicate.'],'Recently I have been busy with work and tend to forget appointments.')
q('skm3-u3-ni-kagiru','「早く寝るのが一番よい」という意味です。疲れた日は、早く寝るに（　　）。',['限る','限って','限りな','限ら'],['に限る gives the subjective best choice.','限って is a connective form and does not complete this sentence.','限りな is not this verb form.','限ら is an unfinished stem.'],'On a tiring day, the best thing is to go to bed early.')
q('skm3-u8-wake-dewa-nai','嫌いだという意味ではありません。嫌いなわけ（　　）ありません。',['では','を','に','と'],['わけではない denies the stated interpretation.','を does not form this negative predicate.','に does not form this construction.','と does not form this construction.'],'It does not mean that I dislike it.')
b['skm3-u4-kawari-ni-exchange']['quiz'][0]['explanations'][3]['reason']='あまり can describe excessive degree leading to a result; it does not express the compensating trade-off intended here.'
b['skm3-fc-tokoro-datta']['quiz'][0]['explanations'][1]['reason']='忘れたところだった would mean had just forgotten; it does not express the averted event required by this context.'
b['skm3-u12-keigo-respect']['quiz'][0]['explanations'][2]['reason']='拝見する is humble for an in-group person viewing something; it does not form the teacher-honorifying ご覧になる pattern.'
for x in p:
 for z in x['quiz']:z['ruleHint']=x['connection']
r.write_text(json.dumps(p,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
